---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Editorial Policy & Archival Standards | Night Lore"
  description="Learn about Night Lore's non-fictional sourcing methodology, dual-perspective analysis, living person privacy protections, and submission moderation process."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-12 border-b border-[var(--color-border)] pb-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono-meta text-[var(--color-text-dim)] mb-3">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-[var(--glow)]">ARCHIVE</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-[var(--glow)]">EDITORIAL POLICY</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">
        Editorial Standards & Archival Policy
      </h1>

      <p class="text-base text-[var(--color-text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
        Night Lore is built on the principle that real-world anomalies deserve factual, multi-perspective documentation. We do not publish creative fiction, exaggerated creepypastas, or unsubstantiated rumors.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 1: Sourcing Standards -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
        <span class="font-mono-meta text-xs text-[var(--glow)] border border-[rgba(255,107,74,0.3)] px-2 py-0.5 rounded">
          SECTION 1.0
        </span>
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text)]">
          Sourcing & Primary Evidence
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="prose-dark text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-text-muted)] space-y-4">
        <p>
          Every case dossier published on Night Lore undergoes rigorous archival verification. We prioritize primary documentation, including:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Official Law Enforcement Logs:</strong> Signed police affidavits, homicide investigation dockets, and dispatch telemetry.</li>
          <li><strong>Judicial & Court Transcripts:</strong> Sworn trial testimony, land deed transfers, and estate probate records.</li>
          <li><strong>Government FOIA Archives:</strong> Defense Intelligence Agency (DIA) contract logs, NTSB accident reports, and FBI vault filings.</li>
          <li><strong>Peer-Reviewed Literature:</strong> Medical polysomnography studies, psychological journals, and audio spectral analysis.</li>
          <li><strong>AI Narration Transparency:</strong> Story audio narrations are synthesized using Google Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS models from tagged documentary scripts to provide accessible, atmospheric listening while preserving exact prose fidelity.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 2: Dual Perspective Framework -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
        <span class="font-mono-meta text-xs text-[var(--glow)] border border-[rgba(255,107,74,0.3)] px-2 py-0.5 rounded">
          SECTION 2.0
        </span>
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text)]">
          The Dual-Perspective Requirement
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="nl-card p-6 border-l-2 border-l-[var(--glow)] mb-4">
        <h3 class="font-mono-meta text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-text-dim)] mb-2">
          MANDATORY EDITORIAL RULE
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text)] leading-relaxed">
          No case is published with a single bias. Every story must feature a comparative analysis presenting both the extraordinary/paranormal claim and the leading scientific or skeptical explanation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-[var(--color-text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
        Whether examining low-frequency electromagnetic fields, sleep paralysis atonia, optical refractions, or intentional financial fraud, Night Lore provides readers with all verifiable facts so they can reach an informed conclusion.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 3: Privacy & Living Non-Public Persons -->
    <section id="privacy" class="mb-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
        <span class="font-mono-meta text-xs text-[var(--glow)] border border-[rgba(255,107,74,0.3)] px-2 py-0.5 rounded">
          SECTION 3.0
        </span>
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text)]">
          Privacy Protection for Living Persons
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="prose-dark text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-text-muted)] space-y-4">
        <p>
          To maintain legal compliance and ethical journalistic integrity:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>No Non-Public Living Suspects:</strong> We never name, identify, or imply guilt toward living private individuals as suspects or perpetrators in unproven supernatural or criminal allegations.</li>
          <li><strong>Anonymization:</strong> Eyewitnesses submitting personal experiences may request total anonymization. Email addresses collected during submission are stored securely and never published.</li>
          <li><strong>Public Figures Exception:</strong> Only individuals named in historical court trials, published academic books, or press releases are cited by name.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 4: Reader Submission Moderation -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
        <span class="font-mono-meta text-xs text-[var(--glow)] border border-[rgba(255,107,74,0.3)] px-2 py-0.5 rounded">
          SECTION 4.0
        </span>
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text)]">
          Submission Moderation Workflow
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="nl-card p-6 font-mono-meta text-xs space-y-3">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-[var(--color-border)] pb-2">
          <span class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">1. SUBMISSION SUBMITTED</span>
          <span class="text-[var(--status-unresolved)]">STATUS: PENDING</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-[var(--color-border)] pb-2">
          <span class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">2. ANTI-SPAM & HONEYPOT FILTER</span>
          <span class="text-[var(--status-witnessed)]">PASSED</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-[var(--color-border)] pb-2">
          <span class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">3. FACT-CHECKING & GEOLOCATION</span>
          <span class="text-[var(--status-ongoing)]">EDITORIAL REVIEW</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">4. ARCHIVAL PUBLISHING</span>
          <span class="text-[var(--status-witnessed)]">STATUS: PUBLISHED</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Contact CTA -->
    <div class="nl-card p-8 text-center bg-[var(--color-surface-2)]">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-2">
        Questions Regarding Our Editorial Standards?
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mb-4">
        Reach our editorial board for corrections, citation updates, or privacy inquiries.
      </p>
      <a href="/submit" class="btn-primary text-xs">
        Contact Editorial Board
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
